The function is already about as cheap as it can be. This version keeps the same checks and the same result, but reads `profile` into a local once. That avoids reloading the member, and the branch hints favor the common case where a profile entry exists.

```cpp
FIT_UINT16 Field::GetNumComponents(void) const
{
    const Profile::MESG* const p = profile;
    if (__builtin_expect(p != NULL, 1))
    {
        const FIT_UINT16 idx = profileIndex;
        if (__builtin_expect(idx < p->numFields, 1))
            return p->fields[idx].numComponents;
    }
    return 0;
}
```